so you did the thing everyone told you  not to do and now you've messed up your  skin barrier maybe you exfoliated too  much maybe you started too many  irritating ingredients at the same time  maybe you've had a cold and you've  rubbed your nose too hard and now your  skin's red and flaky weirdly shiny it's  textured your paws are more obvious  you've got more breakouts and the most  telltale sign of all products that don't  normally sting are stinging maybe even  water is stinging here is a step-by-step  guide on how to fix it this video is  sponsored by bondi sands i'll be using  some of the products from their everyday  skincare range as examples their  products are perfect for dealing with  this situation and not getting into it  in the first place step one stop using  irritating products let's go back and  understand what you did and what's  happening to your skin basically your  skin has 10 to 20 layers of dead cells  on top this is the stratum corneum often  referred to as your skin barrier the  cells in this barrier are dead but that  doesn't mean they don't have an  important function they act as a barrier  between your living cells and the  outside world so this stratum corneum  keeps water from evaporating there are  lots of important processes going on  inside your skin that require enough  water to work water keeps your skin  supple and flexible and it stops it from  cracking the stratum corneum also keeps  irritants and germs out this is its main  function it acts as a form of protection  for the rest of your skin if you  exfoliate too much you end up with a  thinner stratum corneum with less layers  it's like you're giving yourself a mild  chemical burn your barrier ends up  weaker and less effective than it used  to be so now things that didn't used to  irritate now might actually irritate  with this lesser protection so the first  thing to do is to stop sanding back what  barrier you have left so stop using  exfoliating products and the faster you  stop the faster you'll recover it can  take months if you're really unlucky and  you've been ignoring all of the signs so  here are some of the things you need to  stop using firstly chemical exfoliants  this includes alpha hydroxy acids like  glycolic acid and lactic acid also beta  hydroxy acid also known as salicylic  acid also check the ingredients of your  toners as well sometimes they're not  labeled as chemical exfoliants but they  still have these ingredients in them you  also need to stop using physical  exfoliants the obvious ones to look out  for are scrubs and peeling gels but you  might also want to check other things  such as your towels your cloths and  pillowcases if they're a bit rough they  can act like physical exfoliants and  buff away your dead skin cells there's  also shaving if you shave you are  actually taking off some dead skin cells  when you pass the razor over your face  you'll want to be really careful with  this as your skin is trying to recover  also look out for enzyme exfoliants this  includes papaya and pineapple enzymes  sometimes these are in products that are  labeled glow on top of this you'll also  need to stop other irritating products  you might be using your skin has the  ability to repair itself but if you keep  attacking it it can't do that  unfortunately this includes most of the  active ingredients that people hype up  in skin care you'll want to stop using  retinoids these are vitamin a  derivatives like retinol retinaldehyde  and granative retinoid which are found  in regular cosmetic products you might  also want to put a pause on some of the  ones in prescription products like  tretinoin and adaptolene other common  ingredients you might want to stop are  ascorbic acid the classic form of  vitamin c and kojic acid which is a skin  lightening ingredient if you have  products with heavy fragrance that can  also irritate your skin now that you've  paused most of your regular skincare  routine we're up to step two which is  use bland products at this point you  don't want to add irritating products  into your routine you need to give your  skin a break but hydrated skin does heal  better and it helps your skin protect  itself so it's important to pick  products that your skin is less likely  to react to i'd recommend using  different products depending on what  stage of your healing you're at at the  start you'll probably want to use more  oil based and thicker products and  that's because some water-based products  can sting your skin when it's in this  very vulnerable state an example of a  product i'd recommend is the wonder  potion from bondi sands this is a mix of  really nice nourishing oils you can also  use a thicker balm product if you're  after something a little lighter that  you can wear during the day and it won't  look too greasy bondi sands have  released two fragrance-free moisturizers  these both have a really beautiful  texture they sink into your skin and  they protect your skin and hydrate it  without being shiny and greasy and so  they work really well during the day  under makeup or even just under  sunscreen again hydrating products can  sometimes make your skin a little bit  more irritated they can make your skin  barrier more permeable so if your  barrier is already pretty compromised  water-based products tend to sting more  this isn't necessarily bad but it's not  very comfortable so i'd recommend adding  hydrating toners a little bit further  down the line when your skin is a bit  more resilient step three is to use  repairing products now you need to be  really really cautious but your skin can  benefit from adding products with  repairing actives one of these  ingredients is niacinamide bonded sands  has the begin again serum which has ten  percent niacinamide with one percent  zinc the bondi sand serums are in this  really great packaging it's a lot easier  to deal with than a glass dropper bottle  it's much more travel friendly it's  spill proof it's made from recycled  material and it is recyclable the serum  itself has a thicker texture than a lot  of other niacinamide products on the  market so it's a lot easier to apply but  it still spreads really nicely on the  skin there are also some soothing plant  extracts that can help so you might want  to look out for chamomile and oatmeal as  well as centella asiatica extract  sometimes this shows up in the  ingredients list as one of these now  step four is to start again really  slowly once your skin has stopped  stinging as much it's gotten a bit more  resilient and it's recovered you can  start again with your skincare routine  now you need to be super cautious your  skin might not be as recovered as you  think and you don't want to have to go  through this whole process again so i  recommend using really gentle products  to start with don't start off again with  once a week pills or double digit  concentration exfoliants or one percent  retinol as you have now experienced it  can take weeks or months to recover so  you want to have patients going in so  for example you want to start off with  low concentrations don't use high  concentrations just for the sake of  higher concentrations like i said in a  previous video it is a myth that higher  concentrations are always better one  product i really love from the bondi  sands range is the buff and polish  chemical exfoliant this is a really  gentle product it uses gentler  ingredients like lactic acid and  gluconolactone these ingredients are a  bit larger and so their molecules don't  get into the skin as quickly as glycolic  acid so this cuts down on any potential  irritation by a lot with any product you  should try to introduce it really slowly  there are lots of different ways of  doing this so firstly you can try using  less you can measure out your product on  your hand and dilute it with a different  product like a moisturizer to help it  spread you should also start off by  using the product less often so use it  every couple of days instead of every  single day at first when you're starting  you can also wash off the product after  five minutes instead of leaving it  overnight and so that cuts down the  contact time between the ingredient and  your skin also make sure when you're  using irritating products that the rest  of your products are very gentle so use  things with moisturizers and soothing  products also use things with gentle  cleansers the bondi sands freshen up  cleanser is a really gentle fragrance  free low foaming cleanser it's really  hydrating and it clears your skin  without stripping it so like and  subscribe to promise you'll be nicer to  your skin and let me know any other  barry repair tips you might have in the  comments i did a video talking about the  bondi sans everyday skincare range for  the channel check it out via the link in  the description

